  "_comment": [
    "Rig capability: floors, labels and area anchoring \u2014 the registries the rig had NO FILE FOR at all.",
    "",
    "The run-level Integrity census is what turned this up. It reads `floor ls` and `label ls` and",
    "refuses a listing of zero rows, because a census that reads nothing cannot detect damage (H-14).",
    "On the rig both read zero, and the reason was not that the fixture had chosen to have no floors:",
    "it had no floor registry at all, so nothing about floors was expressible here. The reference",
    "instance has both, and every command that reports a floor or a label was rig-untestable.",
    "",
    "The shape is Home Assistant's own. These bytes were produced by booting the rig, running",
    "`floor create` / `label create` / `area create` through hactl, waiting out HA's delayed save and",
    "reading the files back out of the container \u2014 rather than written from memory, which is how the",
    "`aliases` and `minimum` KeyErrors of SPEC-realdata-fixture.md 6 Q1 happened. Timestamps are",
    "frozen so the fixture does not change every time it is regenerated."
